# Telemetry Contract

When writing or changing OpenTelemetry metrics, traces, logs, resource attributes, or OTLP export config, follow the CreaRec contract:

https://github.com/CreaRec/CreaGrafana/blob/main/docs/telemetry-contract.md

Before shipping telemetry changes, fetch or re-read that doc (raw: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CreaRec/CreaGrafana/main/docs/telemetry-contract.md) and verify the change matches it.

## Must follow

- Export **only** to Alloy via OTLP (`OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`). Never point exporters at Loki, Tempo, or Mimir URLs.
- Set resource attributes: `service.name` (kebab-case, no version), `service.namespace`, `service.version`, `deployment.environment` (`production` | `staging` | `local`).
- Bot metrics use the `bot_` prefix and contract names (`bot_updates_total`, `bot_commands_total`, `bot_handler_duration_seconds`, `bot_errors_total`, `bot_inflight`, plus job metrics when applicable). Prefer contract names over parallel custom metrics for the same idea.
- Metric labels: low-cardinality enums only (`result`, `command`, `handler`, `job`, `error_type`, …). Never put `user_id`, `chat_id`, URLs, paths, free-text errors, or trace ids on metric labels.
- Span names follow `bot.handle_update`, `bot.command`, `bot.job.<name>`. On failure: `recordException` + error status. Propagate `trace_id` into logs.
- Export failures must not block business logic (warn and continue).

## Out of scope

Pure business logic with no metrics/traces/logs/OTEL config changes does not need a contract check.
